\item Large bins smooth the distribution but can hide structure.
\item Common choices include Sturges' rule, Scott's rule and
Freedman--Diaconis rule.
\item Advantages: simple, intuitive and useful for EDA.
\item Limitations: appearance depends strongly on bin choice;
not ideal for very small samples or precise density estimation.
\end{itemize}
